WEBVTT

00:05:00.454 --> 00:05:03.913
You see, my sister has been in and out
of the criminal justice system

00:05:03.954 --> 00:05:05.204
for about 30 years.

00:05:06.413 --> 00:05:08.913
You know, we thought
she was “just an addict.”

00:05:09.454 --> 00:05:12.704
Later, we found out that she had
untreated trauma

00:05:12.704 --> 00:05:14.163
from a sexual assault.

00:05:14.954 --> 00:05:17.746
We didn't know what to do,
we didn't know how to help her.

00:05:18.413 --> 00:05:20.329
So when I flew back to Denver,

00:05:20.329 --> 00:05:23.246
I thought about my sister,
I thought about this man,

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:25.954
and I knew we could do better in Denver.

00:05:26.704 --> 00:05:29.579
What intrigued me so much about Eugene

00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:32.288
is that the police
and the mental health crisis team,